  "body": "Two bugs in the release smokes, both found by the first real four-platform dispatch ([run 33870226408](https://github.com/FiredMosquito831/my-claude-code/actions/runs/33870226408)), neither findable from the Windows-only local run that preceded #273.\n\n**Windows passed end to end on that dispatch. Linux, macOS arm64 and macOS x86_64 all failed in the smoke step.**\n\n## 1. A relative binary path did not survive the `cd`\n\nThe POSIX smokes launch the shell from inside the scratch directory. The workflow passes the binary as a path relative to `desktop-shell/`, which resolves to nothing there:\n\n```\n_posix.sh: line 162: src-tauri/target/.../release/MyClaudeCode: No such file or directory\nSMOKE FAIL: the shell died after reading its status\n```\n\nThe message named neither the cause nor the fix. The path is now made absolute immediately after the existence check, before the scratch directory exists. Windows was unaffected because `Resolve-Path` already did this — which is precisely why a local Windows run could not find it.\n\n## 2. The \"the shell ran the stub\" assertion was vacuous — on all four platforms\n\nStep 2 calls the stub twice itself (once for `--print-status`, once to assert the exit code for an unknown flag), so the call log was already non-empty when step 3 began waiting for it. The wait returned immediately.\n\nThat is how three legs printed `ok: the shell ran the stub` and *then* failed on the next assertion: the binary had never started at all. The log is now emptied immediately before the launch, so the wait means \"the **shell** ran it\" rather than \"somebody ran it at some point\". Windows gets the same fix.\n\nThis is the more serious of the two. Bug 1 made three legs fail loudly; bug 2 would have let a leg pass while proving less than it claimed.\n\n## 3. A cosmetic one, found while fixing 2\n\n`Get-Content` on a one-line file returns a string, not an array, so `$calls[0]` was its first character and the Windows smoke reported `ok: the shell ran the stub: -`. Forced into an array.\n\n## Verified\n\n`smoke/windows.ps1` re-run locally against the real release binary: passes, exit 0, and now reports `ok: the shell ran the stub: --print-status` from the shell's own call rather than from step 2's. The POSIX fixes are verified by syntax check and by the path expression itself; their real proof is the re-dispatch after this merges.\n\nNo Python change, so no version bump and no release.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
