     "date": "2026-09-04T12:07:51Z"
    },
    "message": "test(desktop): make the smoke actually wait for the shell to run the stub\n\nTwo bugs the Windows-only local run could not catch, both found by the first\nreal four-platform dispatch (run 33870226408).\n\nThe POSIX smokes launch the shell from inside the scratch directory, so a\nrelative path to the binary -- which is exactly what the workflow passes --\nresolved to nothing there. bash reported \"No such file or directory\" into the\nshell's log and the smoke reported \"the shell died after reading its status\",\nnaming neither the cause nor the fix. The path is now made absolute before\nanything else happens. Windows passed because Resolve-Path already did this.\n\nWorse, and on all four platforms: step 2 calls the stub twice itself, so the\ncall log was already non-empty when step 3 began waiting for it. The wait\nreturned immediately and \"the shell ran the stub\" was asserted even on legs\nwhere the binary never started -- which is how three legs reported that line\nand then failed on the next one. The log is emptied before the launch, so the\nwait now means what it says.\n\nAlso force the Windows call log into an array: Get-Content on a one-line file\nreturns a string, and $calls[0] on a string is its first character, so the\nmessage read \"the shell ran the stub: -\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
